                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' friendly-name='Description' h='49550' id='558' type-v2='text' w='99265' x='368' y='5750'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='2' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='16'>Description of Filters and Metrics</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Filters</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Granularity - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Defines the time interval for data analysis (weekly, monthly, quarterly).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Local Date </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Filters data according to a specific local date or date range.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- SFTP Type -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Selects only vendors that are Central or Legacy SFTP.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Picking App -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Filters data based on the picking application used (Pelican or Godroid).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Is AAA Vendor -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Indicates whether to filter data to include only vendors categorized as AAA.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Is AAA Supermarket - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Filters data to include only those supermarkets classified as AAA.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Has Orders -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Shows only data for vendors that have at least one confirmed order.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Has Stock SFTP Jobs -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Shows only data for vendors that have at least one confirmed Stock SFTP Job.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Has SFTP Promotions -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Shows only data for vendors that have at least one SFTP Campaign Update.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Filter Outliers -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Filter all vendors with high GMV and very few SFTP Jobs for Stock.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- In / Out IDs - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>This field is a switch that makes the following two filters include vendors that are on the provided ID list (IN) or vendors not on that list (OUT).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Chain IDs Filter -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Allows filtering of Chains using a list of Chain IDs separated by commas or spaces.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Vendor IDs Filter -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Allows filtering of Vendors using a list of Vendor IDs separated by commas or spaces.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='14'>Metrics</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Important note: all metrics are calculated at the vendor level. The aggregations of these metrics are weighted averages by GMV. For example, to calculate the score of a country: SUM(Score of each vendor in the country * GMV of each vendor in that country) / SUM(GMV of each vendor in that country). In this way, vendors with higher GMV have a greater weight in each of the metrics (the only 2 metrics exempt from this weighting are &quot;% Not Found / Not Delivered&quot; and &quot;% OOS Failed Orders&quot;).</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- SFTP Score - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>A score from 0 to 100 assigned based on the performance of the Vendor, Chain, Country, etc., in the following 5 metrics: # Every how many days Vendors Update their Stock, Avg. Number of Updates per Day, Ratio # Updates items vs Total Assortment, % Not Found Rate / Items Not Delivered, and % OOS Failed Orders.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- SFTP Score Group - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Based on the SFTP Score, the vendor is assigned to a group. If the score is below 50, it&apos;s Underperforming; between 50 and 79, Neutral; and 80 or above, Overperforming.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>SFTP Score Metrics:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - # Every how many days Vendors Update their Stock - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Frequency of stock updates by a vendor. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: Number of days / Number of days with stock updates.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - Avg. Number of Updates per Day - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Average number of stock updates performed by a vendor per day. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: Nr Jobs to Update Stocks / Number of days.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - % Stock Jobs that Failed -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Percentage of inventory SFTP Jobs that failed. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: Nr Jobs to Update Stocks that Failed / Nr Jobs to Update Stocks.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - Nr Updated Stock Products -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Number of products whose stock was updated via SFTP.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - Ratio # Updates items vs Total Assortment - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Ratio measuring how many products are updated daily compared to the vendor&apos;s total assortment. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: ((Nr Updated Stock Products / Nr Jobs to Update Stocks) / Total Vendor Assortment) * 100.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Others SFTP Metrics:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - # Nr Jobs to Update Stocks - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Number of SFTP Jobs completed to update stock.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Æ  </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> - % of SFTP Vendors -</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Percentage of vendors that has SFTP Jobs.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - % of Failed Lines in CSV Files - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Percentage of erroneous or failed lines in CSV files. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: Nr Updated Stock Products that Failed / Nr Updated Stock Products.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - Avg. Shared Assortment from SFTP - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Perc. of how many products are sent daily compared to the vendor&apos;s total assortment. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: (((Nr Processed Products + Nr Updated Stock Products that Failed) / Nr Jobs to Update Stocks) / Total Vendor Assortment) * 100.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Orders Metrics:</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - % Not Found Rate / Items Not Delivered - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Percentage of ordered items not delivered to the user due to OOS of Confirmed Orders or OOS Failed Orders. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: Unfulfilled item calculations based on different order statuses and items from OOS failed orders, divided by the total relevant ordered items.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>   - % OOS Failed Orders - </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Percentage of orders failed due to out-of-stock (OOS) issues. </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Formula: OOS Failed Orders / Total Orders.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='8' italic='true'>Click again on the icon in the upper right corner to close this window.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='solid' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='1' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                    <format attr='background-color' value='#ffffff' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
